      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I may be wrong, but I beleive he ment that spirits other than Ocean, who end up with presence in the Ocean (ie, through Indomnitable Claim) would not be bale to use Flow Like Water, Reach Like Air on those presence.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I thought the response was addressing moving Presence in to the Ocean with the power, not moving it out of the Ocean. But either way, why is it not allowed?</p>",
